==Battleground==
*10 [[Coffin Zoge]]s spawn, delay 1.33~3.33 seconds<sup>40f~100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Berserkory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 97% HP:
**1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns.
**5 [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 96% HP:
**5 [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 95% HP:
**1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 93% HP:
**5 [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.2 seconds<sup>2f~6f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 92% HP:
**Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 3.33~16.67 seconds<sup>100f~500f</sup>.
**1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Dread Bore]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Quickly try to get rid of the Coffin Zoges with [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] and [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and save money for [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]]. Try using something like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to keep Berserkory at the base. Once the base is hit, Dread Bores will burrow to your base so try to destroy the enemy base quicker.

Alternatively, you can use a unit with low damage to only spawn the Berserkory, then lure him closer to finish him off using [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red units]], leaving the enemy base defenseless for Bahamut to destroy.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Unearthed Artifacts]] stages, Brave Dog's Bone's Japanese name references an idiom. In this case, the name Inu mo Arukeba Bōn (犬も歩けばボーン, "Even a Walking Dog Could be a Bone") is a play on the idiom ''Inu mo arukeba bō ni ataru'' (犬も歩けば棒に当たる, "Even a dog could hit a stick when walking"), used to say that if one takes action rather than sitting still, they may have good luck. However, it can also be interpreted as "Even a dog could be hit with a stick [by a person] when walking", meaning that misfortune can always strike no matter what one does.

